From: ubuntu-rockchip build
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: orangepi-5-plus: more aggressive fan curve

The fan curve inherited from rk3588-orangepi-5.dtsi is very conservative:
cooling-levels tops out at 100/255 (39% duty), and the fan only starts at
55 C, so under sustained load the SoC drifts up towards the 85 C passive
throttling trip while the fan is still barely spinning.

Replace it with a five stage staircase that starts earlier and can reach
full speed, keeping ~20 C of headroom below the 85 C bigcore/GPU trip:

  package temp   fan state   PWM duty
  ------------   ---------   --------
     < 35 C          0        0    (off)
      35 C           1        80   (31%)
      43 C           2        120  (47%)
      50 C           3        160  (63%)
      57 C           4        200  (78%)
    >= 65 C          5        255  (100%)

Hysteresis is 3 C on every trip, comfortably below the 7-8 C spacing, so
the states cannot oscillate. Only the board .dts is touched, so the other
boards sharing rk3588-orangepi-5.dtsi keep the stock curve.

Trade-off: the board idles around 40 C, which is already past the first
trip, so the fan runs continuously rather than ever stopping. Raise the
package-fan0 trip if that is too audible.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-orangepi-5-plus.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-orangepi-5-plus.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-orangepi-5-plus.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-orangepi-5-plus.dts
@@ -117,6 +117,12 @@
 };
 
 &fan {
+	/*
+	 * PWM duty steps, out of 255. The shared OrangePi 5 dtsi tops out at
+	 * 100 (39%), which never lets the fan spin up; go all the way to 255
+	 * so the SoC can be held well below the 85 C throttling point.
+	 */
+	cooling-levels = <0 80 120 160 200 255>;
 	pwms = <&pwm3 0 50000 0>;
 };
 
@@ -256,6 +262,68 @@
 	pwms = <&pwm2 0 25000 0>;
 };
 
+&package_thermal {
+	/* React within half a second instead of one second. */
+	polling-delay = <500>;
+
+	trips {
+		/* Overrides of the two trips defined in rk3588-orangepi-5.dtsi. */
+		package-fan0 {
+			temperature = <35000>;
+			hysteresis = <3000>;
+		};
+
+		package-fan1 {
+			temperature = <43000>;
+			hysteresis = <3000>;
+		};
+
+		package_fan2: package-fan2 {
+			temperature = <50000>;
+			hysteresis = <3000>;
+			type = "active";
+		};
+
+		package_fan3: package-fan3 {
+			temperature = <57000>;
+			hysteresis = <3000>;
+			type = "active";
+		};
+
+		package_fan4: package-fan4 {
+			temperature = <65000>;
+			hysteresis = <3000>;
+			type = "active";
+		};
+	};
+
+	cooling-maps {
+		/* One fan state per trip, so the curve is a plain staircase. */
+		map0 {
+			cooling-device = <&fan 1 1>;
+		};
+
+		map1 {
+			cooling-device = <&fan 2 2>;
+		};
+
+		map2 {
+			trip = <&package_fan2>;
+			cooling-device = <&fan 3 3>;
+		};
+
+		map3 {
+			trip = <&package_fan3>;
+			cooling-device = <&fan 4 4>;
+		};
+
+		map4 {
+			trip = <&package_fan4>;
+			cooling-device = <&fan 5 5>;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
 /* phy1 - M.KEY socket */
 &pcie2x1l0 {
 	reset-gpios = <&gpio4 RK_PA5 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
